      <marc:subfield code="a">Content: It Easter at Princeton and two students, Tom Sullivan and Paul Harris, are a hair&apos;s breadth from solving the mysteries of the Hypnerotomachia Poliphili-a renowned text attributed to an Italian nobleman, a work that has baffled scholars since its publication in 1499. But as their deadline looms, research has stalled-until a long-lost diary surfaces with a vital clue. And when a fellow researcher is murdered just hours later, Tom and Paul realize that they are not the first to glimpse the Hypnerotomachia&apos;a secrets.</marc:subfield>
